{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q009_heme_bundle_fold_not_homology","answer":"No. In stable SCOPe 2.08, the heme-binding four-helical-bundle architecture is fold f.21, SUNID 81344, in class f, “Membrane and cell surface proteins and peptides”. The three named groups are classified as three separate sibling superfamilies under that fold: Transmembrane di-heme cytochromes are superfamily f.21.1, SUNID 81342; Fumarate reductase respiratory complex transmembrane subunits are superfamily f.21.2, SUNID 81343; and Respiratory nitrate reductase 1 gamma chain is superfamily f.21.3, SUNID 103501. The fold’s children endpoint returns those three entries as distinct superfamily children of f.21 rather than a single merged superfamily.

The SCOPe-supported statement is therefore shared fold/topology: a core of four up-and-down transmembrane helices binding one or two hemes between helices. SCOPe superfamily is the level that asserts probable common ancestry, and the f.21 fold has a machine-readable homology warning that levels above superfamily do not imply homology, so f.21.1, f.21.2, and f.21.3 should not be treated as one homologous SCOPe superfamily. That separation also blocks unsafe transfer of exact respiratory-complex role, chain organization, or heme-ligand geometry across the fold: SCOPe comments f.21.2 as containing one family where the fold is in a single chain and another where it is formed by two chains; comments f.21.1 as conserving only three of four heme ligands between its two families; and comments f.21.3 only as a possible link between formate-dehydrogenase gamma subunits and fumarate-reductase FrdC-like structure, not as a fold-wide homology assertion.

This is a SCOPe-negative-at-superfamily conclusion, not proof that the three superfamilies are biologically unrelated, analogs, convergent, or independently originated. A stronger evolutionary claim across f.21.1/f.21.2/f.21.3 would need external sequence evidence, global structural alignment, equivalent heme-ligand/motif comparisons, compatible domain-context evidence, phylogenetic support, or curator literature beyond the retrieved SCOPe hierarchy and comments.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","scop-homology/references/api-usage.md","scop-homology/references/biological-interpretation.md","scop-homology/scripts/scop_compare.py","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=Transmembrane%20di-heme%20cytochromes&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=fumarate-reductase%20respiratory-complex%20transmembrane%20subunits&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=respiratory%20nitrate-reductase%20gamma%20chains&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=heme-binding%20four-helical-bundle&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=Fumarate%20reductase&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=nitrate%20reductase%20gamma&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=cytochrome%20b%20subunit&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=fumarate&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=nitrate&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=gamma&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=heme&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81342","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81343","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/103501","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81344","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81342/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81343/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/103501/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81344/children?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81342/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81342/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81343/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/81343/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/103501/anno